e to others through arts, crafts, games, and more!',NULL,5,0,NULL,NULL,0,0,NULL,0),(487,'Richmond Build Opportunity',11,'09:00:00','15:00:00','Richmond',0,1,1,0,'2023-11-04','habitat@berea.edu','Maria Elkins',1,'Come join the Habitat team this Saturday working on porch repairs for Habitat homeowners!',3,5,0,NULL,NULL,0,0,NULL,0),(488,'Habitat Office Volunteering',11,'15:00:00','17:00:00','Richmond, KY',0,1,1,0,'2023-11-10','habitat@berea.edu','Maria Elkins',0,'Come help out at the Habitat office with cleaning, organizing, and more in support of our wonderful community partner!',2,5,0,NULL,NULL,0,0,NULL,0),(489,'Fall Festival at Irvine Nursing and Rehab',11,'12:45:00','16:00:00','Irvine Nursing and Rehab in Irvine, KY',0,1,1,0,'2023-11-19','agp@berea.edu','Andrea Patton',1,'Join us as we celebrate the fall season with the Irvine community! For this event, we will be engaging, alongside our wonderful participants, in a fall-themed craft, apple cider tasting, hand-painted Polaroid photo opp stations, and more! \r\n\r\nPick-up will be at Alumni Circle at 12:45 pm and we will arrive back on campus by 4:00 pm!  ',NULL,1,0,NULL,NULL,0,0,NULL,0),(490,'Bonfires are Better Together',11,'19:00:00','23:00:00','Corner of Estill and Main St, Stephenson Gravel Parking Lot',0,0,1,0,'2023-11-16','celts@berea.edu','CELTS Admin',1,'As a part of the Better Together campaign, we invite the greater Berea community to come have a s\'mores! Including a raffle and exclusive merchandise. All proceeds are donated to the Berea Food Bank.',NULL,8,0,NULL,NULL,0,0,NULL,0),(491,'All HOP Programs\' Volunteers Fall 2023 ',11,'12:00:00','13:00:00','CELTS',0,0,0,0,'2023-11-14','hop@berea.edu','Frida Jacobo',0,'Test Event \r\nTo register volunteers ',NULL,6,0,NULL,NULL,0,0,NULL,0),(492,'Spooks-Giving',17,'15:00:00','17:00:00','Stephenson Hall Room 212',0,0,1,0,'2023-11-10','bereatutoring@berea.edu','Berea Tutoring',1,'Slime Making, Cookie Decorating, Scavenger Hunt, food, and other games.',NULL,4,0,NULL,NULL,0,0,NULL,0),(493,'Test Event ',17,'12:00:00','13:00:00','Stephenson Hall Room 212',0,1,0,0,'2023-11-15','bereatutoring@berea.edu','Berea Tutoring',0,'A test event ',5,4,0,NULL,NULL,0,0,NULL,0),(494,'Habitat Connect',11,'18:00:00','19:00:00','Stephenson Hall, Activities Room (214)',0,1,1,0,'2023-11-29','habitat@berea.edu','Maria Elkins',1,'Come join the Habitat team and learn about the research they\'ve been working on this semester! There will be pizza and drinks!',NULL,5,0,NULL,NULL,0,0,NULL,0),(495,'2024 KyPolicy Conference ',12,'07:30:00','17:30:00','The Campbell House, Lexington, KY',0,1,0,0,'2024-01-19','heggensa@berea.edu','Sarah Heggen',1,'The Kentucky Center for Economic Policy (KyPolicy) is hosting their annual KyPolicy Conference in Lexington, KY on Friday, January 19th, 9 AM- 4 PM.\r\n \r\nAre you interested in learning more about:\r\n-The Kentucky Legislature?\r\n-Advocacy Work?\r\n-Community Partners?\r\n-Current Issues?\r\n\r\nIf you are still interested, please review the checklist below:\r\n\r\n1. Review the agenda to see discussion topics and format of the conference: https://kypolicy.org/conference-2024/\r\n2. You must make your own arrangements (i.e.: permission from professors, alerting labor supervisors) to miss that Friday\'s classes, labor, and other obligations. \r\n3. We will be leaving at 7:30 AM and returning no later than 5:30 PM. Please eat breakfast beforehand if possible. Lunch is provided.\r\n4. There are limited spots, possibly 12 total in two CELTS vans. Don\'t wait to RSVP if you want to join!\r\n5. RSVP\'s are due by Friday, January 12th by 11:59 PM on CELTSlink, and spots are filled on a first-come, first served basis.\r\n',14,9,1,NULL,NULL,0,0,NULL,0),(497,'Monday Afternoon Programming Week 1',12,'15:30:00','17:30:00','Dominion Senior Living in Richmond, KY',0,1,1,0,'2024-02-12','agp@berea.edu','Andrea Patton',0,'We will be traveling to Dominion Senior Living in Richmond, KY to host programming. Pick-up will always be at 