l be provided to participants. Lunch at Dining Services provided by CELTS, as well as snacks throughout the day. Summary of Event: Participant has successfully completed the 5-hour English Language Learning (ELL) Tutor Training provided by the Hispanic Outreach Program in collaboration with the Madison County Adult Education Program. Attendees of this training enhanced their expertise and proficiency in assisting others with the development of language skills.\r\n\r\n',NULL,6,0,NULL,NULL,0,0,NULL,0),(930,'Café SJ: All About Relations',19,'18:30:00','19:30:00','Stephenson Building, Room 214, Activities Room ',0,0,0,0,'2025-02-19','pwc@berea.edu','Rhea Clayton',1,'Please join People Who Care for our All About Relations Café SJ (Café Social Justice)! We will be watching a short film and discussing healthy relationships. Additionally, we will have finger foods and cookies!',NULL,7,0,NULL,NULL,1,0,NULL,0),(931,'Kentucky Capital Advocacy Day (Feeding Kentucky)',19,'07:00:00','17:00:00','Kentucky Capital',0,1,0,0,'2025-02-18','cochranea@berea.edu','Ashley Cochrane',1,'Join VEPAC and CELTS on a trip to Frankfort on \"Hunger Free Kentucky Day 2025.\" There will be a Rally in the Rotunda, Lunch, group meetings with Berea\'s Representatives and Advocacy Meetings with other representatives. In order to attend RSVP in CELTS Link (link coming soon). ',6,9,0,NULL,NULL,1,0,NULL,0),(932,'Berea Buddies Monday Programming Week 2',19,'17:15:00','20:00:00','Stephenson Hall',0,0,1,0,'2025-02-03','bereabuddies@berea.edu','Ashley Sanchez',0,'K-6 mentoring program.',NULL,2,0,'sancheza','2025-02-17 16:34:50',0,0,NULL,0),(933,'SOS Info Session',19,'15:00:00','18:00:00','Stephenson Connector',0,0,0,0,'2025-03-14','heggensa@berea.edu','Sarah Heggen',0,'Drop-in info session! Third of five, attendance is required at at least one.',NULL,10,0,NULL,NULL,0,0,NULL,0),(934,'SOS Info Session',19,'12:00:00','15:00:00','Stephenson Connector',0,0,0,0,'2025-03-18','heggensa@berea.edu','Sarah Heggen',0,'Drop